WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.630
Cobra Kai has captured the nostalgia of a
multi-generational franchise.

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:08.330
But the characters aren't the only things
viewers find familiar.

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:12.009
Samantha's actress, Mary Mouser, has been
working for years.

00:00:12.009 --> 00:00:14.849
Here's where you might have seen her before.

00:00:14.849 --> 00:00:19.619
Prior to her role as Sam LaRusso on Cobra
Kai, actress Mary Mouser played a recurring

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:22.930
role on Hulu's high-school horror series Freakish.

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:27.199
In that show, a bunch of kids show up for
detention but find themselves fighting off

00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:31.189
killer zombies after a nearby chemical plant
explodes.

00:00:31.189 --> 00:00:35.270
It's like the John Hughes classic, The Breakfast
Club, except the kids in detention aren't

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:37.930
just in trouble -- they're on the menu.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:42.600
Mouser plays Mary Jones, little sister to
Grover, another one of the lead characters.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.030
Those who survive the initial attack must
figure out how to make it out alive without

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:50.010
much in the way of supplies or protection.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:54.010
Mouser only had the role of Mary for one of
the show's two seasons, which is a pretty

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:57.710
good run considering the body count of a zombie
show.

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:02.740
Mary Mouser played the role of Lacey Fleming
on the medical-crime-meets-comedy-drama series

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:06.940
Body of Proof prior to tying her gig as Sam
LaRusso.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:11.000
Before she was Daniel-san's daughter, she
was the nearly estranged daughter of medical

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:16.120
examiner Megan Hunt, a former neurosurgeon
no longer able to operate after suffering

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:18.110
nerve damage in a car crash.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:22.100
Mouser's character was considered a recurring
role for the show's first season, at which

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.130
time Lacey lived with her father.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:29.050
Mouser was promoted to the main cast for the
second and third seasons, as Megan gains joint

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:34.160
custody with her ex-husband, and her relationship
with her daughter slowly evolves, while Lacey

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.090
is shuttled back and forth between parents.

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:42.240
Body of Proof was canceled by ABC in 2013
after three seasons.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.560
There are characters on a TV show who shape
the world of the series with their presence,

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:51.560
and then there are characters who rarely appear,
but whose spirit hangs over everything.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:56.270
Mouser got the opportunity to play one such
character on CBS' long running crime drama

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:57.860
NCIS.

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:02.159
As the deceased daughter, Kelly, of Special
Agent Gibbs, Mouser may have only appeared

00:02:02.159 --> 00:02:07.500
in a few of the series' 400+ episodes, but
she's still arguably one of the more important

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.379
figures of the whole show.

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:14.189
At the beginning of NCIS' run, fans were left
to guess as to why Gibbs has such a tough

00:02:14.189 --> 00:02:17.349
exterior and often secretive personality.

00:02:17.349 --> 00:02:21.849
That changed in season 3, when the show revealed
that he once had a wife and daughter who were

00:02:21.849 --> 00:02:24.299
killed by a member of a drug cartel.

00:02:24.299 --> 00:02:28.659
Gibbs later killed the man in revenge, and
the entire dark episode and the memories of

00:02:28.659 --> 00:02:32.129
his past continue to haunt him throughout
his life.

00:02:32.129 --> 00:02:36.860
Mouser played Kelly in several flashback sequences
throughout the series, most notably in the

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:39.629
episodes "Hiatus Parts I &amp; II."

00:02:39.629 --> 00:02:45.010
While you might not recognize the significantly
younger Mouser right away, NCIS fans may have

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:48.310
sensed Kelly's presence while watching Cobra
Kai.

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:52.750
Typically, when you see that somebody had
a one-episode guest starring role on Criminal

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:57.790
Minds it's either because they played a terrifying
killer, or a terrified victim.

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:02.569
While the series is known for its exceptionally
grisly cases, Mouser's character from the

00:03:02.569 --> 00:03:07.809
season 10 episode "Amelia Porter" survived
with some deep emotional scars, but relatively

00:03:07.809 --> 00:03:09.749
minor physical ones.

00:03:09.749 --> 00:03:14.151
Rebecca is a teenager who becomes one of the
targets of her uncle, Benton Farland, who

00:03:14.151 --> 00:03:19.200
has recently been released from prison after
serving time for the murder of Rebecca's mother.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.389
While Benton didn't kill Rebecca's mother
himself, he manipulated his girlfriend at

00:03:23.389 --> 00:03:26.439
the time, the titular Amelia Porter, to do
so.

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:31.480
Now that he's a free man, he desperately wants
to not only reunite with Amelia, but also

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:35.209
have her recreate the murder he coerced her
into committing.

00:03:35.209 --> 00:03:39.819
Unfortunately for Rebecca, she looks just
like her mother, so Benton kidnaps her in

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:42.059
preparation for his twisted reunion.

00:03:42.059 --> 00:03:44.269
"You don't recognize her?

00:03:44.269 --> 00:03:49.609
It's Rebecca, Miriam's daughter.

00:03:49.609 --> 00:03:52.239
Doesn't she look just like her mother?"

00:03:52.239 --> 00:03:56.489
Thankfully, Amelia isn't as interested in
playing along this time.

00:03:56.489 --> 00:04:01.499
She stalls long enough for the Behavioral
Analysis Unit squad to show up and rescue

00:04:01.499 --> 00:04:05.779
Rebecca, putting Mouser in the special category
of Criminal Minds guest stars whose characters

00:04:05.779 --> 00:04:08.359
didn't die a horrific death.

00:04:08.359 --> 00:04:14.029
Freeform's groundbreaking show The Fosters
centers on Stef and Lena Adams Foster, a married

00:04:14.029 --> 00:04:19.859
couple with a large family composed of their
biological, adopted, and foster children.

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:24.810
Unsurprisingly, the series featured a sizable
cast of characters throughout its five season

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:28.000
run, including Sarah Lewis, played by Mouser.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:32.250
Sarah only has a three episode-arc on the
show, but they make up a pretty memorable

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.690
three episodes.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:38.111
Mouser plays a fellow foster kid who meets
Callie, one of Stef and Lena's charges, in

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:39.490
a therapy group.

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:43.930
Unfortunately for Sarah, she is being groomed
by one of Callie's former foster brothers,

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:48.530
Liam, who Callie knows to be manipulative
and regularly involved with girls who are

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:51.069
far too young for him to be dating.

00:04:51.069 --> 00:04:55.110
After getting wrapped up in Liam's criminal
activity, it looks like Sarah may be at risk

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:59.550
of getting dragged down with Liam, but with
the help of Callie, she's eventually able

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:02.810
to break the spell and turn against him.

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:07.009
Prank calls are all fun and games until the
playful charade starts to take on a life of

00:05:07.009 --> 00:05:09.490
its own and morph into something unsettling.

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:15.840
In "Prank Call," the season 3 episode of the
HBO anthology series Room 104, Mouser stars

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:20.099
as a teenager who stumbles into that lesson
in the worst possible way.

00:05:20.099 --> 00:05:25.440
Each episode of Room 104 focuses on a new
temporary inhabitant of the hotel room that

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:27.189
gives the series its name.

00:05:27.189 --> 00:05:31.500
In "Prank Call," that person is Adrienne,
whose parents have left her alone for the

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:32.500
night.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:35.150
To pass the time, Adrienne makes prank calls.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:40.210
Far from lighthearted jokes, Adrienne's calls
see her adopting personas that are more grown-up

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:41.770
than she's ready for.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:46.419
When she connects with a man named George,
she lets her flirtatious older woman persona

00:05:46.419 --> 00:05:47.770
get away from her.

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:52.520
Before she can put an end to the disturbing
situation, a knock on the hotel room door

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:55.159
escalates the prank to a terrifying degree.

00:05:55.159 --> 00:06:00.949
"Prank Call" is a twisted and often disturbing
episode of TV, but it provides Mouser with

00:06:00.949 --> 00:06:04.479
a multi-layered part to sink her teeth into.

